protocol "PBM — Alzheimer's 1064nm (deep-cortical channel)" {
    id: "30000003-0000-0000-0000-000000000000"
    description: "Whole-vault 1064nm PBM for Alzheimer's / dementia, targeting §1's 1060–1080nm band (Qi/Nizamutdinov 2021: 1060–1080nm, 6 min twice daily, 108 sessions/56 d, MMSE +4.8). RE-AUTHORED 2026-08-26 from the §3 cognitive-enhancement target, which was 8.9× beyond this channel's reach; §1's band is the nearer target OI-HEXTILE-21 identifies. STILL NOT EVIDENCE-GRADE and still not reachable — the shortfall narrows, it does not close. See the notes on the modality block for the exact figures."
    author: "NeurOne"
    version: "2.0"
    readonly: true
    tags: ["pbm", "1064nm", "clinical", "alzheimers"]
    conditions: ["Alzheimer's Disease", "Dementia"]
    references: [["Qi / Nizamutdinov 2021 — double-blind, n=60, 1060–1080nm, 6 min twice daily, 108 sessions/56 d, MMSE +4.8. THIS protocol's source trial: the only §1 trial in the 1060–1080nm band. NOTE: it states no irradiance, so the target below comes from §1's section-level band, not from the trial.", "docs/pbm_neuro_protocols.md#1-alzheimers-disease--dementia--grade-a"], ["PBM protocol database §1 — Alzheimer's / dementia (Grade A), section bands 0.1–0.3 W/cm², 20–75 J/cm², CW acceptable at 1060nm", "docs/pbm_neuro_protocols.md#1-alzheimers-disease--dementia--grade-a"], ["OI-HEXTILE-21 — the 1064nm irradiance wall and the proposal to claim against the AD band rather than the cognitive one", "docs/np_hw_hextile_001.md"], ["Lateralization decision + optical model (retained from Rev 1.1 — no longer load-bearing now the target is whole-vault)", "docs/np_opt_psf_001.md"]]
    duration: 6m

    pbm_transcranial {
        # RE-AUTHORED AGAINST §1 (ALZHEIMER'S), NOT §3 (COGNITIVE ENHANCEMENT).
        # Principal direction 2026-08-26, adopting OI-HEXTILE-21's third option:
        # "claim 1064 nm against the Alzheimer's protocol (1060–1080 nm,
        # 0.1–0.3 W/cm²) rather than the cognitive one."
        #
        # WHAT CHANGED, AND WHAT DID NOT. The commanded parameters are almost
        # unchanged — this block carried `intensity: 100%`, which on this channel
        # meant "all the drive CH_C has": 28 mW/cm² (NP-HW-HEXTILE-001 §4.3.2).
        # Since 2026-09-25 that is stated as the absolute irradiance it always was
        # (OI-HEXTILE-25). What changed at re-authoring is the TARGET, the
        # CONDITION and the ZONE — a claim-and-targeting change, not a power change.
        #
        # THE SHORTFALL NARROWS BUT DOES NOT CLOSE. CH_C gives 28 mW/cm² at 30
        # sites. CW is now CONTINUOUS (OI-HEXTILE-25 — it was capped at 25 % duty
        # until 2026-09-25, 7.0 mW/cm² average), so 28 mW/cm² average:
        #
        #                          irradiance      dose delivered   dose target
        #   §3 cognitive (old)     8.9× short      3.4 J/cm²        60  (18×)
        #   §1 Alzheimer's, 25 %   3.6× short      2.5 J/cm²        20  (7.9×)
        #   §1 Alzheimer's, CW     3.6× short     10.1 J/cm²        20  (2.0×)
        #
        # The target is one the architecture could plausibly reach with a better
        # emitter — which §3's could not, at any tile population (OI-HEXTILE-21:
        # η_wp ≈ 4.8% is an emitter wall, not a power or layout shortfall). It is
        # still NOT reachable today: irradiance is 3.6× under §1's 0.1 W/cm² floor
        # whatever the mode, and 6 min delivers half the 20 J/cm² floor, which
        # 11.9 min of CW would reach.
        irradiance_mw_cm2: 28
        frequency: 0Hz
        # frequency: 0Hz is CW, which §1 permits at 1060nm, and CW now means
        # continuous: 100 % on-time. A CW block takes no duty_cycle.
        zones: ["Vault (excl. Occipital)"]
        # §1's site is "whole-head (bilateral frontal, temporal, parietal +
        # midline)", so the right-lateralized zone this protocol used under the
        # §3 target no longer applies. The PR #210 midline-lateralization
        # reasoning is retained in the references for history but is not
        # load-bearing here: a whole-vault target has no lateralization claim to
        # protect. Matches clinical-01's zone.
        wavelength: "1064nm"
        # Requires a 1064nm-capable (T1-C / smart) module. On a base T1-A build
        # this protocol's PBM channel is unavailable.
        #
        # ⚠ Note OI-PBMCH-04: `wavelength` never reaches the wire on iOS or
        # Windows (NPSessionProtocol+FromDefinition.swift, SessionProtocolCompiler.cs
        # both drop the field), so on those two runtimes this compiles to the same
        # config as a 660_808nm protocol. That is a pre-existing cross-platform
        # defect, not one this re-authoring introduces, but it bears on any claim
        # made about what this protocol delivers.
    }
}
